{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>That which was.</b> The deed of Elohim is on one path, and that which was already is — its matter is the same, and there is the like of it, and that which is yet to be already was the like of it. \"Is pursued\" [נרדף] is the stationary [element]; he marked it with the word הוא [is], and it [הוא] is between past and future. The matter is that Elohim sought from time that it be pursued — time pursuing after time, without cessation, for the time that passed returns standing, and that which is yet to be returns like the past, and the time recurs. And if it is divided into future time and past, this is a matter that will be clarified by the sphere: every part of it pursues after the central point, which is the solid center [מוצק], and it is called מוצק on account of the pressure [צוק] of place. The first line is the breadth, and likewise the breadth — there is no solid center beneath it. And the part that was in the east returns in the west, and vice versa, and the place of the sphere's motion has no beginning from which it starts, for every beginning is an end and every end is a beginning. And the pursued is the solid center. And so he has explained to us that every deed of Elohim is on one path."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The text is a single long run-on sentence with minimal punctuation in the source; I have inserted periods and commas at the natural syntactic breaks. 'מוצק' (solid center) and 'צוק' (pressure) are a wordplay preserved literally. The reference to 'the sphere' (גלגל) and its geometric properties is left as delivered, without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:22.170128953Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}